  "description": "PAQBAO crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C46 H35 Er1 F12 N3 O16 Yb2 1+,C18 H10 Er1 F18 O9 1-,1.25(C6 H14). From the CIF bond table, Yb4 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 7 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Yb1 (Yb) has 7 O neighbors; Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.574-3.697 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.33-102.53°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C64H45Er2F30N3O25Yb2.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
